  - local competence estimation
  - dynamic combination
  - regressor selection
abstract: >
  Python implementation of the MINE framework for dynamic regressor selection,
  originally proposed by Moura et al. (2021) in MATLAB. MINE trains a homogeneous
  Bagging ensemble and applies competence-based dynamic selection using eight
  local competence measures with GA-optimized weights. Three combination strategies
  are evaluated: MINE-S (dynamic selection), MINE-W (dynamic weighting), and
  MINE-WS (weighted selection). This port was developed as the main baseline for
  comparison with the DREAM framework in a doctoral thesis on dynamic ensemble
  selection for regression.
